<Defs>

	<!--THERMIC MECHANICS:
		-The THERMIC LANCE is a rifle that can be attuned extreme heat, extreme cold... or both.
		-THERMIC starts off as as a basic rifle that does rudimentary damage, with no bonuses. It has half the lifespan of an attuned lance, but it can be attuned with any temperature.
			-The damage values and stats are incredibly low, on part with a standard assault rifle or carbine.
			-It is charged with shocksap in this state.
		-When the THERMIC LANCE is imbued with embersap or cryosap, it gains elemental attunement to fire or ice, respectively. This attunement increases most stats, and grants the projectiles elemental properties.
			-The THERMIC LANCE (IGNITED) gains the following:
				-Fast projectile output and speed
				-Lowered accuracy and high spread
				-Projectiles deal burning damage
				-Alt fire mode that ignites a small area (cooldown)
			-The THERMIC LANCE (FRIGID) gains the following:
				-High accuracy and lowered spread
				-Lowered projectile output and speed
				-Projectiles deal frost damage
				-Alt fire mode causes hypothermia in a small area (cooldown)
		-Imbuing the weapon with that same sap once more will further improve it, granting them the following effects:
			-THERMIC LANCE (INFERAL):
				-All stats affected (both good and bad)
				-Gains and additional ability: "Hellfire Barrage", which fires a barrage of 30 non-stop searing shots. Cannot be stopped.
			-THERMIC LANCE (GLACIAL):
				-All stats affected (good and bad)
				-Gains an additional ability: "Deep Freeze", which stuns a large area for several seconds. Takes two days before cooldown ends.
			
		-HOWEVER, if the THERMIC LANCE is imbued with CHROMASAP, it will gain both stages of the ignited and frigid variants. This will only occur if the imbuement occurs while completely drained.
		-The THERMIC LANCE *can* be imbued with the opposing sap, but this will only lower it's 'temperature' by one stage. This means a total of FOUR saps are needed to change one Stage 2 THERMIC LANCE to the other STAGE 2.
			-For example, the process of obtaining an INFERAL THERMAL LANCE is:
				THERMAL LANCE (dormant) -> Infuse with Embersap -> Create THERMAL LANCE (IGNITED) -> Infuse with Embersap -> Created THERMAL LANCE (INFERAL) (2 embersaps used)
				...however, if you want to turn that into a THERMAL LANCE (FRIGID), the process would be:
				THERMAL LANCE (INFERNAL) -> Infused with Cryosap -> Create THERMAL LANCE (IGNITED) -> Infuse with Cryosap -> Create THERMAL LANCE (dormant) -> Infuse with Cryosap ->  THERMAL LANCE (FRIGID)
				... THEREFORE, IT IS HIGHLY SUGGESTED YOU LET YOUR LANCE SIMPLY RETURN TO THE DORMANT STAGE ITSELF.
			-Because of this, it is very helpful to have a few THERMIC LANCES on hand, in case the need or desire for heat/cold-based weaponry changes.
		-Per stage, the THERMIC LANCE has a shorter lifespan than most other lithic weapons, but it won't enter a 'drained' state like most others; instead, it will go back to it's prior "temperature". This can be avoided by infusing it with it's proper sap.
			-However, the stage 1 (dormant) rifle will enter a drained state if it's lifespan runs out. It will take a significant amount of shocksap to recharge... but can also accept Embersap or Cryosap at this stage.
				-Additionally, this is the only stage that can accept Chromasap
		-Like most other Lithic weapons, the THERMIC LANCE has some basic rules it follows:
			-It will never truly expire
			-Lifespans are extremely long, and at full charge it can easily last over a year, if not two.
		-The theme of the weapon is pretty straightforward.
			This weapon is based around temperature - specifically, fire and ice.
		-->

</Defs>
